import{_ as t,o as a,c as i,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 149 | Realm Refinement · Boundary-Breaking Realm | Predatory Faction vs. Symbiotic Faction","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 149 | Realm Refinement · Boundary-Breaking Realm | Predatory Faction vs. Symbiotic Faction","no":149,"module":1,"tags":["Realm","Boundary-Breaking Realm","Predatory Faction","Symbiotic Faction","Path Comparison"],"related":["14-Unified Cultivation Realm Classification","04-Anti-Predation Core Treatise","05-Myriad Races Progress Basic Program"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0149_模块1-破界境-掠夺派vs共生派对比.md","filePath":"en/0149_模块1-破界境-掠夺派vs共生派对比.md"}'),r={name:"en/0149_模块1-破界境-掠夺派vs共生派对比.md"};function n(s,e,l,d,c,u){return a(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-149-boundary-breaking-realm-predatory-faction-vs-symbiotic-faction-detailed-comparison" tabindex="-1">Entry 149 | Boundary-Breaking Realm: Predatory Faction vs. Symbiotic Faction Detailed Comparison <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-149-boundary-breaking-realm-predatory-faction-vs-symbiotic-faction-detailed-comparison" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 149 | Boundary-Breaking Realm: Predatory Faction vs. Symbiotic Faction Detailed Comparison&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 1 · In-Depth Realm Refinement | Baseline references: Documents 14, 04, 05</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-the-same-cross-boundary-door-two-worldviews" tabindex="-1">Introduction: The same cross-boundary door, two worldviews <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-the-same-cross-boundary-door-two-worldviews" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: The same cross-boundary door, two worldviews&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Boundary-Breaking Realm puts the two civilizational paths&#39; fundamental divergence on the same stage for the first time. Per the Unified Cultivation Realm Classification (Document 14), boundary-breaking = anchor-free cross-plane travel, operating the plane membrane. When this &quot;cross-boundary right&quot; falls into the <strong>Predatory</strong> hand, it is a license to open territory and plunder; when it falls into the <strong>Symbiotic</strong> (Anchor Symbiotic Civilization) hand, it is a work pass for building roads and networks. This entry puts the two paths&#39; complete differences in the Boundary-Breaking Realm on the table, making the divergence tangible, comparable, and judgeable.</p><p>The six top-level axioms running through the text are precisely the symbiotic faction&#39;s point-by-point counter-propositions to the predatory: the anti-predation axiom says no to &quot;cross-boundary harvesting&quot;; the republican axiom of Myriad Races says no to &quot;plane lords&quot;; the collective ascension axiom says no to &quot;solitary ascension&quot;; the causal self-discipline axiom says no to &quot;overstepping interference&quot;; the law-first axiom says no to &quot;plot-style cheats.&quot; Per Anti-Predation Core Treatise (Document 04) and Myriad Races Progress Basic Program (Document 05), this entry does a systematic comparison; the universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-overview-comparison-table" tabindex="-1">I. Overview Comparison Table <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-overview-comparison-table" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Overview Comparison Table&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Predatory Boundary-Breaker</th><th>Symbiotic Boundary-Breaker</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Crossing purpose</td><td>Discover and occupy resource planes</td><td>Build roads, prospect, ecological interconnection</td></tr><tr><td>Resource acquisition</td><td>Extract, enslave, harvest in-boundary stock</td><td>Develop increments, relay knowledge</td></tr><tr><td>Relation to in-boundary beings</td><td>Treat planes as private property, beings as appendages/prey</td><td>Protect beings first, then talk about channels</td></tr><tr><td>Filing supervision</td><td>None, the strongman does as he pleases</td><td>Alaya five gates full-process trace</td></tr><tr><td>Failure consequence</td><td>Plane collapse, civilizational regression</td><td>Simulation rehearsal + guardianship, cost controllable</td></tr><tr><td>Ceiling</td><td>Plane overlord, eventually overthrown by a stronger one</td><td>Plane guardian, can perpetually promote to World-Creation/Origin</td></tr><tr><td>Mind requirement</td><td>None, the strong takes all</td><td>Anti-predation stance + ethics review</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="ii-crossing-motivation-territory-desire-vs-transportation-network" tabindex="-1">II. Crossing Motivation: Territory Desire vs. Transportation Network <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-crossing-motivation-territory-desire-vs-transportation-network" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Crossing Motivation: Territory Desire vs. Transportation Network&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Predatory&#39;s first motivation for boundary-breaking is &quot;this plane is mine now.&quot; Crossing = prospecting resources, drawing boundaries to be king; the plane membrane is for him a gash to &quot;tear open and snatch a handful.&quot; Its psychological root is the sentient-origin greed-shortcut inner demon — treating the cosmos as a cake to be divided.</p><p>The Symbiotic&#39;s first motivation for boundary-breaking is &quot;does this road connect.&quot; Crossing = prospecting law compatibility, recording plane information, assessing whether a channel is worth building. The plane membrane is for him an interface &quot;needing protection and maintenance.&quot; He cares about roads, not territory.</p><p>This divergence seems abstract, but in practice is: every Predatory crossing, cosmic stock decreases by a fraction; every Symbiotic crossing, Myriad Races&#39; passages increase by one.</p><h2 id="iii-resource-logic-consuming-stock-vs-making-increments" tabindex="-1">III. Resource Logic: Consuming Stock vs. Making Increments <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-resource-logic-consuming-stock-vs-making-increments" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Resource Logic: Consuming Stock vs. Making Increments&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Predatory: after crossing, directly mine off-plane veins, drain plane origin energy, essentially <strong>zero-sum predation</strong>. Document 04 already argues its efficiency ceiling — the more it preys, the drier the preyed plane, eventually nothing to prey, strong ones fight each other to death.</p><p>Symbiotic: after crossing only does &quot;knowledge relay&quot; and &quot;law compatibility&quot;; resources come from the home plane&#39;s incremental circulation (Origin Three-Basic). Off-plane beings and ecology are preserved as-is, even benefit from the channel. Essentially <strong>positive-sum symbiosis</strong>.</p><p>One judgment criterion suffices: a boundary-breaker comes back from crossing, did he bring back a pile of others&#39; ore, or a map and a set of techniques? The former is predatory, the latter is symbiotic.</p><h2 id="iv-relation-to-beings-lord-vs-guardian" tabindex="-1">IV. Relation to Beings: Lord vs. Guardian <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-relation-to-beings-lord-vs-guardian" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Relation to Beings: Lord vs. Guardian&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Predatory treats off-plane beings as chives — raise them, harvest regularly. Plane lords and beings are master-and-slave; history has proven countless times this relationship inevitably erupts in rebellion.</p><p>The Symbiotic treats off-plane beings as neighbors — first assesses the impact of crossing on them, confirms &quot;no causal disturbance&quot; before acting. Guardians and beings are service-and-trust. The Plane Transcendent&#39;s (Origin Realm, see Entry 157) &quot;the greater the power the greater the responsibility&quot; is precisely the apex of this logic.</p><h2 id="v-supervision-and-ceiling-unruled-vs-networked" tabindex="-1">V. Supervision and Ceiling: Unruled vs. Networked <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-supervision-and-ceiling-unruled-vs-networked" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Supervision and Ceiling: Unruled vs. Networked&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Predatory boundary-breakers have no filing, no supervision, no accountability — seemingly free, actually fragile: once a stronger one appears, his &quot;territory&quot; immediately changes hands — this is the predatory system&#39;s &quot;extremely high protagonist uniqueness dependence&quot; dead spot, always relying on new overlords overthrowing old ones, civilization spinning in place.</p><p>Symbiotic boundary-breakers are constrained by the Alaya five gates — seemingly not free, actually stable: ability recorded by the network, experience reused network-wide, status accumulated by contribution. Strong ones emerge in numbers rather than one family monopolizing, precisely the 20% Activation Strategy&#39;s institutional goal.</p><h2 id="vi-typical-ending-comparison" tabindex="-1">VI. Typical Ending Comparison <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-typical-ending-comparison" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Typical Ending Comparison&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Predatory boundary-breaker&#39;s ending: either backlashed by laws in cross-boundary predation, or overthrown in endless internal strife; the &quot;territory&quot; he guarded collapses with his death, beings return to the sea of suffering</li><li>Symbiotic boundary-breaker&#39;s ending: step by step promoting to World-Creation, Origin, Multiverse, becoming a permanent node of the Myriad Races network; the road he built continues to benefit beings after him</li></ul><h2 id="vii-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">VII. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#vii-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VII. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Universal infinite backstop</strong>: the universal equal infinite law establishes that every being inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing have a guarantee, strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose, predation naturally loses meaning</li><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: the Predatory burns cross-boundary genius into &quot;short-lived overlords&quot;; the Symbiotic nurtures it into &quot;perpetual builders&quot;; the former is the greatest waste</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: this entry&#39;s thesis — cross-boundary harvesting and cross-boundary road-building, one character difference, two civilizational paths</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-style cross-boundary strong ones run amok for a while by protagonist uniqueness; Heng Yuan Zhou boundary-breakers perpetuate by network and contribution, extremely low protagonist uniqueness dependence</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the symbiotic path defaults all Myriad Races can break boundaries; the predatory path only tolerates one lord</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the symbiotic faction&#39;s roads, maps, and techniques are fully open; the predatory&#39;s &quot;territory&quot; is never open</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Boundary-Breaking Realm is a touchstone: the door is the same door, but the direction across determines whether one is an overlord or a road-builder. The Predatory faction walks the cosmos smaller and smaller; the Symbiotic faction walks the cosmos bigger and bigger. Myriad Races&#39; choice is never &quot;whether to cross boundaries,&quot; but &quot;after crossing, do you build a road or dig a grave.&quot;</p><p>In the final analysis, the Boundary-Breaking Realm Predatory vs. Symbiotic comparison described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./14-修炼境界统一划分.html">14-Unified Cultivation Realm Classification</a> · <a href="./04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">04-Anti-Predation Core Treatise</a> · <a href="./05-万族共进基本纲领.html">05-Myriad Races Progress Basic Program</a> · <a href="./17-位面至高强者标准.html">17-Plane Transcendent Standard</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',30)])])}const p=t(r,[["render",n]]);export{g as __pageData,p as default};
